book.summary.title=Contents

book.guide.introduction.title=Welcome, Evoker
book.guide.introduction.text=The Evoke Book brings Hex objects to life.\n\nSome blocks are Hex items: when evoked, they turn into Hex Creatures that follow you and help with everyday tasks, such as harvesting crops, storing items in chests or lighting the way.\n\nThis book has three bookmarks:\n- My Creatures: the Hex Creatures you have evoked\n- Guide: tips and an introduction to the mod\n- Hex Creatures: a page for each creature, with its origin item, cost, upkeep and characteristics
book.guide.evoking.title=Evoking
book.guide.evoking.text=Place a Hex item and use the primary action of the Evoke Book on it. The nearest Hex item comes to life.\n\nHex Creature limit: at first you can have 1 Hex Creature at a time. Each new Hex Creature you evoke for the first time is registered in the Hex Creatures bookmark and raises your limit by 1.\n\nWhat is stored in the block goes with the creature: the contents of a chest go to the Chest Spider's inventory, and the armor and weapon of a Hex Mannequin are equipped on the creature.
book.guide.life_essence.title=Essence of Life
book.guide.life_essence.text=Evoking a Hex Creature costs Essence of Life. The cost is taken from your inventory at the moment of the evocation. The Essence of Life spent is kept inside the creature.\n\nSome creatures spend this Essence over time, but it is only spent while the creature is loaded in the world.\n\nIf the creature has Essence of Life in its inventory, it refills itself. Creatures with upkeep also pick up Essence of Life dropped on the ground nearby and keep it in their inventory.\n\nWhen the storage reaches zero, the creature turns back into its origin block.
book.guide.essence_tray.title=Essence Tray
book.guide.essence_tray.text=The Essence Tray is used to store Essence of Life. When a Hex Creature that spends Essence of Life drops to half of its storage and there is a tray with Essence of Life nearby, it stops what it is doing and goes to the tray to take some.\n\nPlace trays near where your creatures work so the essence never runs out.
book.guide.wands.title=Evoke Wands
book.guide.wands.text=Wands give orders to your Hex Creatures.\n\n- Primary: select a creature, or send the selected creatures to a location, where they stay\n- Charged Primary: select all creatures\n- Secondary: deselect a creature, or make the selected creatures follow you\n- Charged Secondary: deselect all creatures\n\nEach wand has a limit of selected creatures and a reach.\n\nHex Mannequin and Hex Homunculus carry items: select one and use Primary on a chest, or crouch and use Primary on another of your creatures. It stores what it carries there and waits where it was for more. Choose a second container and it carries items from the first to the second in a loop.
book.guide.behaviour.title=Behaviour
book.guide.behaviour.text=By default, Hex Creatures follow you. When sent to a location with a wand, they stay there and start working: the Hex Broom wanders around collecting items, the Arcane Codex explores the chests nearby, and so on.\n\nIf you get too far away, most creatures teleport back to you.\n\nCreatures that work with items always look for the nearest chest, so keep chests close to where they work.
book.guide.managing.title=My Creatures
book.guide.managing.text=The My Creatures bookmark shows all your Hex Creatures and how many you have out of your current limit.\n\n- Essence of Life: how much is left in the creature's storage and, for creatures with upkeep, how long it lasts\n- Pencil: edit the names of the creatures; press Save to confirm\n- Checkbox: shows the name above the creature\n- Despawn: removes the creature, dropping its Hex item, its inventory and the Essence of Life left in its storage
book.guide.reverting.title=Reverting
book.guide.reverting.text=Look at one of your Hex Creatures and use the primary action of the Evoke Book to turn it back into its block, right where it stands.\n\nThe equipment of a Hex Mannequin goes back to the mannequin, and the inventory of a Chest Spider goes back to the chest. The Essence of Life left in the creature's storage drops on the ground.\n\nThe block needs free space under the creature.
book.guide.tips.title=Tips
book.guide.tips.text=All Hex Creatures have an inventory, some need you to crouch before interacting.

